From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=81ngel=20Ren=C3=A9?=
 <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:43:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: report the clamped OUTPUT buffer size
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

S_FMT on the OUTPUT queue caps the bitstream buffer at the variant's
CPB size, but hands the application back the size it asked for. The
buffers then come out smaller than the format says.

GStreamer asks for width * height for a 4K H.264 stream (8294400
bytes), the MFC v15 caps it at 7 MiB, and v4l2h264dec gives up with
"buffer size 7340032 is smaller then negotiated size 8294400" and
"Failed to allocate required memory". Return the clamped size, as the
default branch already does.

On the Pixel 7 a 3840x2160 High profile clip then decodes in full and
its frames match FFmpeg's software decoder bit for bit.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
index d26bafe4d..cfc1694e7 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
@@ -476,6 +476,7 @@ static int vidioc_s_fmt(struct file *file, void *priv, struct v4l2_format *f)
 			ctx->dec_src_buf_size = buf_size->cpb;
 		else
 			ctx->dec_src_buf_size = pix_mp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage;
+		pix_mp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage = ctx->dec_src_buf_size;
 		pix_mp->plane_fmt[0].bytesperline = 0;
 		ctx->state = MFCINST_INIT;
 		ret = 0;
